  "solution": {
    "brief": "Basic Wasp discrete aggregation: define geometry, create connections, build Part, set Rule, run stochastic Aggregation",
    "principle": "\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Tutorial 02 (wasp_02_rule_grammar) is the direct sequel to this tutorial, extending the rule definition step to cover multi-rule grammar — specifying multiple distinct rules that control which connections can mate and in what orientation. Where tutorial 01 introduces a single bidirectional rule pair, tutorial 02 teaches how to define a grammar of rules governing connection compatibility across a part vocabulary.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Tutorial 05 (wasp_05_collider) introduces collider and containment as an intermediate extension of the basic aggregation workflow first established here — Wasp collision detection against boundary BRep geometry constrains growth within a defined volume. Learners progressing from this beginner tutorial toward intermediate Wasp usage will encounter collider/containment as a key growth-control mechanism in the tutorial sequence.",
